WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.343
- Even right now as we speak,

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:04.140
there are some 10, 12, 14 year olds

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.423
that's being groomed right now.

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.350
Most people end up the way they are

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.360
because they're a product
of their environment,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.140
and that's 1000% true.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.278
- [Announcer] If you were alone in a room

00:00:15.278 --> 00:00:18.283
with a former gang member,
what would you ask?

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:19.410
- Do you ever feel like
you had a normal life?

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.550
- Have you ever been to jail?

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.260
- Have you ever killed someone?

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.258
- What is your favorite song?

00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:27.180
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.410
- My name is Sabrina.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.430
What's your name?

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.480
- I'm Tyrone, Sabrina

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:32.434
- Tyrone.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.267
- So like, just curious

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.435
can I get a little bit of your background?

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.933
- Start from the beginning.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.520
- Well, I'm a former gang member.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.143
Was part of the CRIP gangs.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.750
Being in LA and being in
the gang neighborhoods,

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.073
there's no way to get around it,

00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:46.590
either you're gonna be
a part of it as a victim

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.390
or you're gonna be a
part of it as a member.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.251
So I chose to be a member.

00:00:50.251 --> 00:00:51.383
That was the safest route.

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.216
In the inner city of LA

00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:54.332
you have gang members on every block.

00:00:54.332 --> 00:00:55.260
So if you're a part of a certain gang

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.020
that kind of gave you a sense of security.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.690
- What age did you start
out as a gang member?

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.730
- I started running with 'em around 12,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.820
but actually got fully accepted around 14.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.220
- When you started in the gang,
was it something cause like,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.230
you know, you wanted
to feel like Scarface?

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.820
- A lot of us grew up in the neighborhood,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.220
and our brothers and
sisters are gang members.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.806
- Right.

00:01:15.806 --> 00:01:16.828
- And we wanna be like that.

00:01:16.828 --> 00:01:17.813
- Right.

00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:18.829
- We're not looking for that out.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.310
We want that reputation
that my brother got.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.592
He went to jail.

00:01:21.592 --> 00:01:23.640
You know, you might find it crazy,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.089
but a lot of guys growing
up, looking forward to that.

00:01:27.089 --> 00:01:28.093
(beep)

00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:29.394
- You know, getting them stripes.

00:01:29.394 --> 00:01:30.510
That shows that you're
serious about that life.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.470
- Being a gang member,

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.540
do you ever feel like
you had a normal life?

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.340
- At the time, I felt normal.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.850
Being a gang member at that
time, it was like an honor,

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.530
a badge of honor honestly.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.450
- What was the initiation process like?

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.530
- Painful.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.790
Getting jumped in.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.580
You may end up fighting anywhere
between four to six guys.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.630
They're cussing you.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.420
They're literally beating you up.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.370
But soon as it's over,
as soon as it stops,

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.767
they're shaking hands and hugging you,

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:58.650
and you are now officially
a part of this family.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.270
A lot of people don't understand

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.990
why they're trying to hurt you

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.850
if you're trying to be a part of the gang,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.970
but it's basically to see
what type of man you are.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.020
You know, can you take some of the things

00:02:08.891 --> 00:02:09.990
that may happen to you in this situation?

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.120
- Do you have any gang related tattoos?

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.170
- Yeah, I have several.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.280
- Do you have a favorite?

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.290
- Probably my gang name.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.810
They call me by my nickname, Tee Mac.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.960
On the left it says Tee,
T-E-E going down the back,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.600
and it has a Mac on the other side, M-A-C.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.510
To this day, I still
get called by that name.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.592
- For the record, that's
a really cool nickname.

00:02:29.592 --> 00:02:34.500
- So what is a normal day in
the life of a gang member?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.570
- First thing is on your
mind is making some money.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.560
We were going to school.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.880
We were able to make money in school

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.280
selling weed at school,
selling dope at school.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.970
That became a easy way for
a lot of us to make money

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.740
when we couldn't get
money from our parents

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.710
or if it was just hard times at home.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.910
- Have you ever been to jail?

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.710
- Yeah, been to jail a few times.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.913
- Was it regarding your drugs or the gang?

00:02:54.913 --> 00:02:59.452
- Drugs and as well as
robbery and stuff like

00:02:59.452 --> 00:03:00.285
that came to gang banging.

00:03:00.285 --> 00:03:02.134
- Have you ever experienced anyone

00:03:02.134 --> 00:03:03.090
like overdosing over drugs?

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.820
- I've experienced people
overdosing on drugs.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.580
I've experienced a lady going in labor.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.413
- Oh, wow.

00:03:09.413 --> 00:03:11.460
- Actually having a child on the streets

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.040
at the time that she was
trying to purchase some crack.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:14.873
- Wow.

00:03:15.748 --> 00:03:16.581
- You know, just for a little bit of dope.

00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:19.260
- Did that ever make you
wanna stop selling drugs

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.870
or was it kind of just like,
I need my money too, like?

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.100
- You have to convince yourself,

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.560
well, this is what it's
gonna take for me to survive.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.520
You're thinking to yourself,

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.600
well, I'm not making them do it.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.433
- Right.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.274
- You know, this is their choice.

00:03:30.274 --> 00:03:31.920
You give yourself all these
reasons to keep doing it

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.180
without blaming yourself.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.790
- Do you remember the first
time that you held a gun?

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.350
- I can remember clear as day.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.140
When I graduated middle school,
right after my graduation,

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.060
clear as day I went to the neighborhood,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.310
and the guy that's
considered my big homie,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.633
his gift to me as a
graduation gift was that 22

00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:51.270
and $200 worth of crack cocaine.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.280
People look at that as
a negative, like who?

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.360
What type of gift is that?

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.373
Some crack and a gun,
but living that life,

00:03:57.373 --> 00:03:59.040
that was a great gift.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.572
- Yeah.

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:02.400
- I felt protected even
though it was a little 22.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.440
- Have you ever killed someone?

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.500
- No, not to my knowledge, no.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.580
- That's good.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.310
Have you experienced a
close call with death?

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.610
- I mean, in the 80s, drive-by
shootings was real prevalent.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.340
You can be standing
outside, daytime, nighttime

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.300
it just didn't matter.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.410
They were there that fast

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.296
and start shooting at us

00:04:21.296 --> 00:04:22.129
to where we would get to running,

00:04:22.129 --> 00:04:25.110
and bullets are literally
hitting walls in front of us,

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.100
passing us up.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.100
So those are some scary
situations in drive-bys

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.100
because you have no idea
where the bullets are going.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:32.970
- Yeah.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.450
- Do you feel like you've
become desensitized to violence?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.110
- I think I'm more sensitive
to violence that's being done

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.320
because as cold hearted as you need to be

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.495
a lot of us had remorse,
but we couldn't show that.

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:48.475
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:48.475 --> 00:04:50.159
We couldn't show that to the homies.

00:04:50.159 --> 00:04:52.410
We need to be as non remorseful
and as evil as they are.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.640
- Do you ever feel like you were hiding

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.550
under some sort of facade of masculinity?

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.233
- Oh, of course, of course.

00:04:59.214 --> 00:05:00.625
You have to develop this character.

00:05:00.625 --> 00:05:01.650
You have to become more tougher.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.810
You know, you have to become
more, what they call harder,

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.870
less remorseful and kind of like not care.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.640
And so a lot of times
you have to walk around

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.800
with your chest out, and there were times

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.610
where I had to put up
that real tough guy facade

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.070
to maybe, you know, scare
the hell outta somebody.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.770
- How did being in a gang
affect your relationships

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.860
with friends, families, partners?

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.050
- I literally lived a double life.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.660
There's a situation
where we had participated

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.880
in a drive-by shooting.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:30.900
So I walk in the house,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.270
and the situation that I participated in

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.010
is actually on the news.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.500
My mom's on the phone, and
she's watching this story

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.290
on the news, and I'm listening
to her tell her friend

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.390
oh, it's a shame how these
kids killing one another.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.850
And I'm sitting there
thinking to myself like,

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.889
wow, she don't have no idea

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.140
that her son was just a part of that.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.191
And I even get chills
talking about that right,

00:05:52.191 --> 00:05:53.870
even right now as I speak about it.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.140
- In the movies, what do they get wrong

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.460
and what do they get right?

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.740
- When you look at at gang
movies, it's about violence.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:05:59.573
It's about robbing.

00:05:59.573 --> 00:06:01.252
It's about killing.

00:06:01.252 --> 00:06:02.251
Everything is negative.

00:06:02.251 --> 00:06:03.934
But the side the movies
miss is that camaraderie

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.570
that brotherly and that family love.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.190
Everybody there has your back.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.900
Even on financial things

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:12.180
and things that you need to get done

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.190
that you might not be able
to get from your family.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.951
They'll take care of,

00:06:15.951 --> 00:06:16.784
they'll take care of that for you.

00:06:16.784 --> 00:06:18.120
That really is your family.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:20.220
- I'm a native of Southern California,

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.650
so I have ties to gang culture.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.030
When you say it means love,

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.614
but they're going against
each other like other gangs,

00:06:26.614 --> 00:06:28.530
I don't see that being love.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.380
- Well, that's because there
are reasons that only we,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.412
that you can only
understand as a gang member

00:06:33.412 --> 00:06:36.030
on why I'm against my brother.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.020
- I totally understand.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.860
But at the same time, gang
culture wasn't intended for that.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.720
It was a vigilante type
thing intended to protect

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.574
like it was in the Bay
Area back in the day

00:06:45.574 --> 00:06:46.613
with the Black Panthers.

00:06:46.613 --> 00:06:47.446
You're going against each other.

00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:49.380
It just defeated the purpose to me.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.872
Do you agree with that,
cause that's not cool?

00:06:51.872 --> 00:06:52.950
- I agree with it to a certain extent.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.080
The black gangs in
particular were reinvented

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.114
to protect our own neighborhoods.

00:06:57.114 --> 00:06:57.947
- Exactly.

00:06:57.947 --> 00:07:00.060
- Few people know that CRIP stands for

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.890
Community Resistance In Progress.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.395
- Yes.

00:07:03.395 --> 00:07:05.392
- So back then, that's what
it was supposed to represent.

00:07:05.392 --> 00:07:07.620
- Is this something that can be fixed?

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.900
- I don't think that it
can ever totally be fixed

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.530
because the hatred and
the dislike runs deep

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.910
from a long time ago.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.153
Some of us can look at it and and say,

00:07:17.153 --> 00:07:17.986
well, no, they killed my brother.

00:07:17.986 --> 00:07:19.434
- Yeah.

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:20.450
- Or they killed my homie.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.283
That that would never be forgiven.

00:07:21.283 --> 00:07:22.116
- It needs to be another way.

00:07:22.116 --> 00:07:23.430
That's just, that's all I'm saying.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.290
- No, there's nothing good about it.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.370
- Yeah.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.340
- What was like your
moment of like awakening

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.380
where you were like, oh
dang, I gotta switch it up.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.030
- There was no particular moment.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.770
You don't so much get out of gangs,

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.350
even when you get it
in your 40s, your 50s.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.350
You're still considered
part of that family.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.660
You're just doing different
things in your life.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.180
Eventually I went to college.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.190
I ended up moving to Oklahoma City.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.830
I ended up being a police
officer working in the schools.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.592
I could use my experience
to show kids that, you know,

00:07:52.592 --> 00:07:54.990
you could get out of this (beeping).

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:55.823
- Are you still a cop or?

00:07:55.823 --> 00:07:57.030
- Not a cop no more.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.220
Wouldn't go back into life
for nothing in the world.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.710
To me, the police officer
have their own gangs as well.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.750
Police Academy is kind
of like a brotherhood

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.830
just like gangs,

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:08.010
and certain things have to
stay within those walls.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:10.680
I got to see how they really felt.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.180
It could be some racial slurs.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.190
It could be some negative
things said about us.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.700
With me being a part of that
life that they hated so much,

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.650
a lot of things that
they said affected me.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.530
It bothered me because that was my life.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:25.050
- Did you have to arrest any
of your like own homeboys

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.482
and stuff like that?

00:08:26.482 --> 00:08:28.530
- Never, because I was never
a police officer in LA,

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.030
and I would've never done that.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.210
The rule of the streets were
more than important to me

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.208
than anything.

00:08:34.208 --> 00:08:35.400
If I had to arrest a gang
member as a police officer,

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.300
I would've quit.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.804
- Dang.

00:08:37.804 --> 00:08:39.537
You know, because I'm not,
that's not what I was there for.

00:08:39.537 --> 00:08:43.380
- Are you still in contact
with anyone from your gang?

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:44.550
- Yeah, daily.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.730
Just because you change your
life, you don't turn your back

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:50.250
on your friends or guys
that are still caught up.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.720
You still have to stay connected

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:56.310
because this is a lifetime involvement.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:57.990
- Do you regret having been in a gang?

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.330
- The only regrets I
have from being in a gang

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:03.570
would be the hurt that I caused people

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.880
because at that time you don't realize

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.860
the things that you were doing,

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.300
how bad it's affecting people

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.740
and how bad it could hurt people.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.980
My regret would be that
I helped this multiply.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:16.590
I helped it spread worldwide.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.270
I mean, gang banging is in places

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.920
that you would never think now.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.070
- Do you think gang
culture will ever die out?

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.630
- Honestly, no.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.870
Because even right now as we speak,

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:31.380
there are some young 10, 12, 14 year olds

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.709
that's being groomed right now.

00:09:33.709 --> 00:09:34.590
Most people end up the way they are

